      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.35,
      "end_seconds": 287.17,
      "duration_seconds": 12.82,
      "text": "okay, thank you, you can get dressed. Putting it all together, I don't have a clear answer today: benign prostate enlargement is possible, and so is a a urine infection"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.72,
      "end_seconds": 291.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "is it it dangerous, um, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.82,
      "end_seconds": 297.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like benign prostate enlargement"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.98,
      "end_seconds": 321.92,
      "duration_seconds": 14.94,
      "text": "I'm going to put you on tamsulosin, 400 micrograms, once a day after food, long term. You take it by mouth. That's for urinary symptoms. Come back after the results. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.5,
      "end_seconds": 324.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
